\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Abide with me; fast falls the eventide;
\par The darkness deepens; Lord, with me abide!
\par When other helpers fail, and comforts flee,
\par Help of the helpless, O abide with me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Swift to its close ebbs out life's little day;
\par Earth's joys grow dim, its glories pass away;
\par Change and decay in all around I see:
\par O Thou who changest not, abide with me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I need Thy presence every passing hour;
\par What but Thy grace can foil the tempter's power?
\par Who like Thyself my guide and stay can be?
\par Through cloud and sunshine, O abide with me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I fear no foe, with Thee at hand to bless;
\par Ills have no weight, and tears no bitterness;
\par Where is death's sting? where, grave, thy victory?
\par I triumph still, if Thou abide with me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Hold Thou Thy Cross before my closing eyes;
\par Shine through the gloom, and point me to the skies;
\par Heaven's morning breaks, and earth's vain shadows flee:
\par In life, in death, O Lord, abide with me!
\par 
\par \f1 
